#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store Qiskit objects to disk so you can continue where you left off"
msgstr "I-store ang mga Qiskit object sa disk para matuloy ang iyong ginagawa"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save circuits to disk"
msgstr "I-save ang mga circuit sa disk"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code sa pahinang ito ay ginawa gamit ang mga sumusunod na requirements.\n"
"Inirerekomenda namin ang paggamit ng mga bersyong ito o mas bago pa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use [QPY serialization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) to save your circuit to file. QPY files store the full Qiskit circuit object and will be compatible with newer versions of Qiskit (although not necessarily with older versions of Qiskit).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Gamitin ang [QPY serialization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) para i-save ang iyong circuit sa file. Iniimbak ng mga QPY file ang buong Qiskit circuit object at magiging compatible sa mga mas bagong bersyon ng Qiskit (bagaman hindi tiyak na compatible sa mas lumang mga bersyon ng Qiskit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To demonstrate, the following cell creates a simple quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Para ipakita, ang sumusunod na cell ay gumagawa ng simpleng quantum circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To save this file to disk, use the `qpy.dump` function. You can also save a list of circuits.\n"
msgstr "Para i-save ang file na ito sa disk, gamitin ang `qpy.dump` function. Maaari ka ring mag-save ng listahan ng mga circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit is now saved to the file `test.qpy`. If you restart your Python kernel, you can re-load the circuit using the `qpy.load` function. Note that this always returns a list of circuits, even if you only serialized one circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang circuit na ito ay naka-save na ngayon sa file na `test.qpy`. Kung i-restart mo ang iyong Python kernel, maaari mong i-re-load ang circuit gamit ang `qpy.load` function. Tandaan na palagi itong nagbabalik ng listahan ng mga circuit, kahit isa lang ang na-serialize mo.\n"

